{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1847 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "6d062ba697d9746967d7cf429467ac2c20adfa43db20e307b99712647dfc7e0d" :edb/db-before-t 1846 :edb/db-after-t 1847 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535159 50 #inst "2026-10-08T18:18:11.240Z" 13194139535159 true] [17592186078358 1020 #edb/ref 17592186334581 13194139535159 true] [17592186078359 1020 #edb/ref 17592186334578 13194139535159 true] [17592186078360 1020 #edb/ref 17592186334564 13194139535159 true] [17592186078360 1020 #edb/ref 17592186334571 13194139535159 true] [17592186078862 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535159 true] [17592186078862 1100 "For $x > 2$, find $f^{′}(x)$ if $f(x) = ∫_{2}^{\\sqrt{x}}\\frac{1}{2 - t^{2}}dt$." 13194139535159 false] [17592186078862 1100 "For $x>2$, find ${f}^{′}(x)$ if $f(x)={\\int }_{2}^{\\sqrt{x}}\\frac{1}{2-{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.$" 13194139535159 true] [17592186078862 1145 "To compute ${f}^{′}(x),$ we first make the substitution $u=\\sqrt{x}$ and then we apply the chain rule, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}{\\int }_{2}^{\\sqrt{x}}\\frac{1}{2-{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}{\\int }_{2}^{u}\\frac{1}{2-{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe integrand is continuous on $[2,u],$ and so by FTC II we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2-{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2-{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2-(\\sqrt{x})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}(2-x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334564 1017 #edb/ref 17592186334565 13194139535159 true] [17592186334564 1089 "q-117291" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334564 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535159 true] [17592186334564 1100 "Find ${f}^{′}(0)$ if $f(x)={\\int }_{x}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{e}^{1-{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.$" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334564 1113 #uuid "5345f4d0-20b2-5008-8103-b715a5705623" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334564 1145 "Here, both the lower and upper limits contain a variable. However, to apply FTC II, we need the variable to be on the upper limit only. So, we can split the integral into two integrals, and rewrite them so that in both cases the variable is on the upper limit. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{x}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{e}^{1-{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{x}^{a}{e}^{1-{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{a}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{e}^{1-{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{a}^{x}{e}^{1-{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{a}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{e}^{1-{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is any constant number between $x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\nThe integrand ${e}^{1-{t}^{2}}$ is continuous for all $t,$ so applying the FTC II gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-{\\int }_{a}^{x}{e}^{1-{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{a}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{e}^{1-{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\int }_{a}^{x}{e}^{1-{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\int }_{a}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{e}^{1-{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-{e}^{1-{x}^{2}}+\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({\\int }_{a}^{u}{e}^{1-{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-{e}^{1-{x}^{2}}+(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x){e}^{1-{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =-{e}^{1-{x}^{2}}-{e}^{1-{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =-{e}^{1-{x}^{2}}-{e}^{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we used the substitution $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\nFinally, we can compute ${f}^{′}(0).$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(0) & =-{e}^{1-{0}^{2}}-{e}^{{sin}^{2}⁡0}\\operatorname{sin}⁡0 \\\\  & =-{e}^{1-0}-0 \\\\  & =-e.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334565 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334566 13194139535159 true] [17592186334565 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334567 13194139535159 true] [17592186334565 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334568 13194139535159 true] [17592186334565 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334569 13194139535159 true] [17592186334565 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334570 13194139535159 true] [17592186334565 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535159 true] [17592186334565 1041 "selection" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334565 1104 #edb/ref 17592186334566 13194139535159 true] [17592186334565 1110 #uuid "6eecd04d-b3de-5834-bf4c-562fcb4318f6" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334566 1034 "-e" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334566 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535159 true] [17592186334566 1111 #uuid "8e9a46e6-fbd7-5405-9402-e9fc0047ccf1" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334567 1034 "2+5e" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334567 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535159 true] [17592186334567 1111 #uuid "dc5f80ec-3a43-5624-bc0b-43e47a7494b5" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334568 1034 "1" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334568 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535159 true] [17592186334568 1111 #uuid "ac6f4488-6cc5-538f-a565-b8ac6cffef44" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334569 1034 "3-4{e}^{2}" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334569 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535159 true] [17592186334569 1111 #uuid "723b769e-a6bd-53f1-bd52-58f138ebd19c" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334570 1034 "0" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334570 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535159 true] [17592186334570 1111 #uuid "39ea09d4-69b3-5406-8754-367858191628" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334571 1017 #edb/ref 17592186334572 13194139535159 true] [17592186334571 1089 "q-117292" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334571 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535159 true] [17592186334571 1100 "Find ${f}^{′}(0)$ if $f(x)={\\int }_{-{e}^{2x}}^{x}\\sqrt[3]{{t}^{3}+1}\\,\\text{d}t.$" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334571 1113 #uuid "47a1e353-0abf-5596-bc63-479c1e9efffa" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334571 1145 "Here, both the lower and upper limits contain a variable. However, to apply FTC II, we need the variable to be on the upper limit only. So, we can split the integral into two integrals, and rewrite them so that in both cases the variable is on the upper limit. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-{e}^{2x}}^{x}\\sqrt[3]{{t}^{3}+1}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{-{e}^{2x}}^{a}\\sqrt[3]{{t}^{3}+1}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{a}^{x}\\sqrt[3]{{t}^{3}+1}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{a}^{-{e}^{2x}}\\sqrt[3]{{t}^{3}+1}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{a}^{x}\\sqrt[3]{{t}^{3}+1}\\,\\text{d}t,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is any constant number between $-{e}^{2x}$ and $x.$\n\nThe integrand $\\sqrt[3]{{t}^{3}+1}$ is continuous for all $t,$ so applying the FTC II gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-{\\int }_{a}^{-{e}^{2x}}\\sqrt[3]{{t}^{3}+1}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{a}^{x}\\sqrt[3]{{t}^{3}+1}\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\int }_{a}^{-{e}^{2x}}\\sqrt[3]{{t}^{3}+1}\\,\\text{d}t)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\int }_{a}^{x}\\sqrt[3]{{t}^{3}+1}\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({\\int }_{a}^{u}\\sqrt[3]{{t}^{3}+1}\\,\\text{d}t)+\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{3}+1} \\\\  & =-(-2{e}^{2x})\\sqrt[3]{{u}^{3}+1}+\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{3}+1} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2x}\\sqrt[3]{(-{e}^{2x})^{3}+1}+\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{3}+1} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2x}\\sqrt[3]{1-{e}^{6x}}+\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{3}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we used the substitution $u=-{e}^{2x}.$\n\nFinally, we can compute ${f}^{′}(0).$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(0) & =2{e}^{2(0)}\\sqrt[3]{1-{e}^{6(0)}}+\\sqrt[3]{{0}^{3}+1} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt[3]{1-1}+\\sqrt[3]{1} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334572 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334573 13194139535159 true] [17592186334572 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334574 13194139535159 true] [17592186334572 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334575 13194139535159 true] [17592186334572 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334576 13194139535159 true] [17592186334572 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334577 13194139535159 true] [17592186334572 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535159 true] [17592186334572 1041 "selection" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334572 1104 #edb/ref 17592186334575 13194139535159 true] [17592186334572 1110 #uuid "4f7fba06-d2fb-5a65-b4a9-dbf68dcbd802" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334573 1034 "3" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334573 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535159 true] [17592186334573 1111 #uuid "35d734a7-fa06-598e-bc02-367c8cda50a2" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334574 1034 "3\\sqrt[3]{1-e}-2" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334574 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535159 true] [17592186334574 1111 #uuid "12c0e594-5c1d-559b-849f-55cab6bd1351" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334575 1034 "1" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334575 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535159 true] [17592186334575 1111 #uuid "08383a5e-262e-5ecf-a09a-8ac9d8a98df8" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334576 1034 "2\\sqrt[3]{1-e}+3" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334576 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535159 true] [17592186334576 1111 #uuid "04d22ae3-2fba-515f-8199-72512c411d1a" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334577 1034 "0" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334577 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535159 true] [17592186334577 1111 #uuid "108d0a5a-a0fc-593b-9c3f-43c46566491e" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334578 1017 #edb/ref 17592186334579 13194139535159 true] [17592186334578 1089 "q-333583" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334578 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535159 true] [17592186334578 1100 "Find ${g}^{′}(x)$ for $g(x)={\\int }_{{e}^{x}}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t.$\n\n${g}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334578 1113 #uuid "d4b317c5-e5ec-5e4f-8ea0-05929d43147f" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334578 1145 "To compute ${g}^{′}(x),$ we first make the substitution $u={e}^{x}$ and then we apply the chain rule, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}{\\int }_{{e}^{x}}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}{\\int }_{u}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe limit $u$ is located on the lower limit. To apply FTC II, we need the variable to be on the upper limit. Using the properties of definite integrals, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}{\\int }_{u}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(-{\\int }_{3}^{u}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}{\\int }_{3}^{u}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by FTC II, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}{\\int }_{u}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\cdot (-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}{\\int }_{3}^{u}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(({e}^{x})^{2})) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{2x})) \\\\  & =-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{2x}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334579 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334580 13194139535159 true] [17592186334579 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535159 true] [17592186334579 1041 "field-1" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334579 1104 #edb/ref 17592186334580 13194139535159 true] [17592186334579 1110 #uuid "83489642-2ffa-5db2-a79f-78b742327bab" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334580 1034 "-e^x\\sin(e^{2x})" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334580 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535159 true] [17592186334580 1111 #uuid "b6c9710b-2cc6-58b2-887f-9f935486e343" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334581 1017 #edb/ref 17592186334582 13194139535159 true] [17592186334581 1089 "q-75220" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334581 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535159 true] [17592186334581 1100 "Let $f(x)={x}^{2}+5x+1.$ Find ${g}^{′}(5)$ given the function is defined by $g(x)={\\int }_{x}^{7}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.$" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334581 1113 #uuid "04689b09-69a7-501a-b2fc-c0ba3b87804e" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334581 1145 "In this example, the variable limit $x$ is located on the lower limit. To apply FTC II, we need the variable to be on the upper limit. Using the properties of definite integrals, we can write\n\n$$\ng(x)={\\int }_{x}^{7}({t}^{2}+5t+1)\\,\\text{d}t=-{\\int }_{7}^{x}({t}^{2}+5t+1)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by FTC II, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}{\\int }_{x}^{7}({t}^{2}+5t+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-{\\int }_{7}^{x}({t}^{2}+5t+1)\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\int }_{7}^{x}({t}^{2}+5t+1)\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-({x}^{2}+5x+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the value of ${g}^{′}(5),$ we substitute $x=5$ in the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(5) & =-({5}^{2}+5\\cdot 5+1) \\\\  & =-(25+25+1) \\\\  & =-51\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334582 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334583 13194139535159 true] [17592186334582 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334584 13194139535159 true] [17592186334582 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334585 13194139535159 true] [17592186334582 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334586 13194139535159 true] [17592186334582 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334587 13194139535159 true] [17592186334582 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535159 true] [17592186334582 1041 "selection" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334582 1104 #edb/ref 17592186334583 13194139535159 true] [17592186334582 1110 #uuid "59b24bc6-6bec-5d87-a059-3b98d93075da" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334583 1034 "{g}^{′}(5)=-51" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334583 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535159 true] [17592186334583 1111 #uuid "910d7a2d-690e-54d1-8815-c962dfda7f44" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334584 1034 "{g}^{′}(5)=43" 13194139535159 true] [17592186334584 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535